     remain vested in the Licensor.

2.3  RESERVATION OF RIGHTS
     All rights not expressly granted herein are reserved by the Licensor.
     No rights are granted by implication, estoppel, or otherwise.

================================================================================
                         3. LICENSE GRANT AND SCOPE
================================================================================

3.1  GRANT OF LICENSE
     Subject to strict compliance with this Agreement, the Licensor grants to
     Authorized Users a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable
     license to:

     (a) Access and operate the Software for official Ministry of Groove
         business purposes only;

     (b) Generate, process, and store classified operational data within
         authorized security parameters;

     (c) Execute authorized functions including but not limited to:
         • Personnel Dossier management
         • Media Archive operations
         • Frequency Monitoring and analytics
         • Directorate-level command functions (clearance-dependent)

3.2  SCOPE RESTRICTIONS
     This license is restricted to:

     (a) Internal deployment within Ministry of Groove secure infrastructure;

     (b) Authorized personnel with validated security clearance levels:
         - AGENT: Basic operational access
         - OPERATOR: Enhanced system functions
         - DIRECTOR: Full administrative authority

     (c) Operational environments meeting MOG-SPEC-2026 security standards.

================================================================================
                    4. PROHIBITED ACTIVITIES (STRICTLY ENFORCED)
================================================================================

4.1  UNAUTHORIZED DISTRIBUTION
     The Software, in whole or in part, SHALL NOT be:
     (a) Sold, leased, rented, sublicensed, or commercially exploited;
     (b) Distributed to third parties without written authorization;
     (c) Made available on public networks, repositories, or platforms;
     (d) Transmitted across unsecured communication channels.

4.2  REVERSE ENGINEERING
     Authorized Users SHALL NOT:
     (a) Decompile, disassemble, or reverse engineer the Software;
     (b) Attempt to derive source code from object code;
     (c) Bypass, disable, or circumvent security mechanisms;
     (d) Modify authentication protocols or access controls;
     (e) Extract cryptographic keys or session tokens.

4.3  UNAUTHORIZED MODIFICATION
     Prohibited activities include:
     (a) Creating derivative works without Directorate approval;
     (b) Removing or altering copyright notices, watermarks, or classifications;
     (c) Integrating with unauthorized third-party systems;
     (d) Deploying modified versions to production environments.

4.4  DATA EXFILTRATION
     STRICTLY PROHIBITED:
     (a) Exporting classified data to unauthorized systems;
     (b) Screenshotting, photographing, or recording sensitive displays;
     (c) Transmitting operational data to personal devices or accounts;
     (d) Retaining access credentials after termination of authorization.

================================================================================
                         5. SECURITY OBLIGATIONS
================================================================================

5.1  ACCESS CONTROL
     Authorized Users must:
     (a) Maintain credential confidentiality;
     (b) Implement multi-factor authentication where available;
     (c) Report suspected security breaches within 15 minutes;
     (d) Terminate sessions when operational presence is discontinued.

5.2  AUDIT COMPLIANCE
     All system interactions are subject to:
     (a) Comprehensive logging and monitoring;
     (b) Periodic security audits;
     (c) Compliance verification by Directorate authorities;
     (d) Forensic investigation of anomalous activities.

5.3  INCIDENT REPORTING
     Security incidents must be reported to:
     • Primary: security@ministryofgroove.internal
     • Emergency: +SEC-URGENT (secure channel)
     • Directorate: director@mog.gov (Level 4+ incidents)

================================================================================
                    6. TERMINATION AND REVOCATION
================================================================================

6.1  GROUNDS FOR TERMINATION
     This license terminates immediately upon:
     (a) Violation of any provision herein;
     (b) Revocation of security clearance;
     (c) Termination of employment or operational status;
     (d) Unauthorized disclosure of Classified Information;
     (e) Detection of security compromise or insider threat indicators.

6.2  POST-TERMINATION OBLIGATIONS
     Upon termination, Authorized Users must:
     (a) Cease all Software access immediately;
     (b) Return or destroy all copies, documentation, and derivatives;
     (c) Confirm destruction via MOG-FORM-26B;
     (d) Submit to exit interview and systems audit.

6.3  SURVIVAL
     Sections 2, 4, 7, 8, and 9 survive termination indefinitely.

